  "script": "This factory off-roader started at about $350,000 and gave up nearly four inches of ground clearance compared with the one it replaced. That\u2019s the Mercedes-AMG G63 4x4\u00b2. In 2022 Mercedes brought back the Squared formula but built it on the AMG G63 instead of the old G550. Its four-liter twin-turbo V8 makes 577 horsepower and 627 pound-feet of torque. The nine-speed automatic drives all four wheels full time, and when the trail gets steep you can drop the transfer case into low range. You get three lockers. Up front, gears at the wheel hubs let AMG move the axle shafts higher without giving up independent suspension. You can call it a mall crawler, but Mercedes rates it to wade through 35.8 inches of water. Would you actually take that factory off-roader up a rock ledge where every inch of clearance counts, or would you leave it on pavement?",
